# The image build context is this directory, the tool's own, so nothing belonging to
# another tool and no .git is ever sent to the daemon. What is left to exclude is this
# tool's tests and deployment scripts, none of which the image needs.
#
# An allow-list naming exactly the two paths deploy/Dockerfile COPYs, rather than a
# deny-list. A deny-list has to be kept in step with .gitignore by hand, and it had
# already drifted: it still excluded a state file the bot stopped writing. This cannot
# go stale, because anything not named here is excluded by construction.
#
# This governs what is *transferred*, not what ends up in the image: the Dockerfile
# COPYs two named files, so nothing here can leak into the result. The smoke test in CI
# is what checks the image contents.
*
!copilot-review-bot.sh
!deploy/entrypoint.sh
